00:16:29,864 --> 00:16:30,865
And they were...

281
00:16:31,616 --> 00:16:33,201
too far away.

282
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:37,705
Even so.

283
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:41,042
Even if it was dark and they were far away,

284
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:46,756
how could you not recognise your own parents?

285
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:59,309
You really think this is going to work?

286
00:16:59,310 --> 00:17:00,853
Just stick to the plan.

287
00:17:01,854 --> 00:17:03,773
Don't go off-book and ruin it.

288
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:06,359
Keep your mind on the kids. Only the kids.

289
00:17:07,068 --> 00:17:08,152
Jeez.

290
00:17:13,074 --> 00:17:14,825
I'm sorry!

291
00:17:15,368 --> 00:17:17,245
I'm so sorry!

292
00:17:22,375 --> 00:17:24,877
I know it's too late,

293
00:17:26,462 --> 00:17:28,256
but we want...

294
00:17:28,798 --> 00:17:30,799
to compensate you somehow.

295
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:35,971
Of course, no amount of compensation can wash away your grief.

296
00:17:35,972 --> 00:17:38,640
We'll do whatever it takes.

297
00:17:38,641 --> 00:17:41,935
If there's anything you want,

298
00:17:41,936 --> 00:17:43,353
please just tell us.

299
00:17:43,354 --> 00:17:44,896
Mom, he thinks you...

300
00:17:44,897 --> 00:17:46,857
Anything I want?

301
00:17:49,193 --> 00:17:51,486
It's not my mom. She just...

302
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:53,321
My gosh! Why are you getting so mad?

303
00:17:53,322 --> 00:17:55,740
Please. We're sorry. We were wrong.

304
00:17:55,741 --> 00:17:57,993
We'll compensate you for everything.

305
00:17:57,994 --> 00:18:00,245
They're just kids.

306
00:18:00,246 --> 00:18:02,414
They made a mistake...

307
00:18:02,415 --> 00:18:04,374
because they didn't know...

308
00:18:04,375 --> 00:18:06,751
any better.

309
00:18:06,752 --> 00:18:07,962
The kids?

310
00:18:13,009 --> 00:18:14,343
Which one of them?

311
00:18:15,011 --> 00:18:16,137
- What? - What?

312
00:18:17,513 --> 00:18:18,764
Well...

313
00:18:20,016 --> 00:18:21,516
My daughter said...

314
00:18:21,517 --> 00:18:23,351
she was in the passenger seat.

315
00:18:23,352 --> 00:18:24,853
She wasn't driving.

316
00:18:24,854 --> 00:18:26,813
The one driving was Min...

317
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:29,734
- Min... - It wasn't my daughter!

318
00:18:30,735 --> 00:18:32,193
It was their family car to begin with,

319
00:18:32,194 --> 00:18:33,862
and Ye Ji was driving her dad's car...

320
00:18:33,863 --> 00:18:35,031
Nonsense!

321
00:18:35,906 --> 00:18:38,658
It's all on this crazy woman and her daughter.

322
00:18:38,659 --> 00:18:40,327
My kid wasn't driving.

323
00:18:40,328 --> 00:18:42,787
- She doesn't even know how. - My gosh. Then,

324
00:18:42,788 --> 00:18:44,372
- why did you clean up the mess? - What?

325
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:46,082
I have evidence. I got it all on video.

326
00:18:46,083 --> 00:18:47,250
- I... - Are you crazy?

327
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:49,085
- You've completely lost it. - Here.

328
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:50,086
I've got it right here.

329
00:18:50,087 --> 00:18:51,463
- Ouch! - Here it is.

330
00:18:51,464 --> 00:18:52,715
Here.

331
00:19:06,437 --> 00:19:09,023
Is that my brother they're carrying?

332
00:19:12,902 --> 00:19:14,903
It was just a tragic accident.

333
00:19:14,904 --> 00:19:15,988
Please...

334
00:19:16,405 --> 00:19:19,074
Please don't hurt the kids.

335
00:19:19,075 --> 00:19:20,076
Please...

336
00:19:23,954 --> 00:19:25,038
Mom!

337
00:19:25,039 --> 00:19:26,581
Ye Ji.

338
00:19:26,582 --> 00:19:27,832
- Mom! - Ye Ji.

339
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:29,502
Your brother.

340
00:19:31,003 --> 00:19:32,880
I'm the only one...

341
00:19:33,506 --> 00:19:36,384
who knows where he is.

342
00:19:45,434 --> 00:19:47,103
(Calling: Babe)

343
00:20:16,966 --> 00:20:19,552
Why the heck aren't they here yet?

344
00:20:49,665 --> 00:20:50,666
It...

345
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:52,501
It won't move.

346
00:20:57,590 --> 00:20:58,966
Come here.

347
00:21:17,193 --> 00:21:18,194
What's wrong?

348
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:25,325
- What is it? - Quiet down.

349
00:21:25,326 --> 00:21:27,369
- What... - Stay still for a second.

350
00:21:28,078 --> 00:21:29,078
What is it?

351
00:21:29,079 --> 00:21:30,080
Honey.

352
00:21:30,748 --> 00:21:33,124
- Step aside. - What are you doing?

353
00:21:33,125 --> 00:21:35,461
When I ram the car, dodge.

354
00:21:54,104 --> 00:21:56,231
When I give the signal, run as fast as you can.

355
00:21:56,232 --> 00:21:57,482
What?

356
00:21:57,483 --> 00:21:58,526
Have you lost your...

357
00:21:59,401 --> 00:22:01,778
We're going to get ourselves killed.

358
00:22:01,779 --> 00:22:03,864
If he finds the body, we'll all be dead anyway.

359
00:22:05,366 --> 00:22:08,202
Are you saying the body is actually buried down here?

360
00:22:25,219 --> 00:22:26,303
Now!

361
00:22:26,929 --> 00:22:27,930
Now?

362
00:22:28,931 --> 00:22:30,306
- Move. - What are you doing?

363
00:22:30,307 --> 00:22:31,599
- Are you crazy? - Move!

364
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:32,935
What are you doing?

365
00:22:35,271 --> 00:22:37,022
(Brake support, Collision evasion)

366
00:22:37,857 --> 00:22:39,190
What the? What's going on? Why...

367
00:22:39,191 --> 00:22:40,900
- Hey. - Wait.

368
00:22:40,901 --> 00:22:42,068
Not at this timing!

369
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:43,820
- Jeez! - Reverse it.

370
00:22:43,821 --> 00:22:44,822
Back it up!

371
00:22:45,573 --> 00:22:46,574
Back up!

372
00:22:48,909 --> 00:22:49,994
What's wrong with this?

373
00:22:54,248 --> 00:22:55,249
Hold on.

374
00:22:58,669 --> 00:23:01,130
Goodness, sir. What are you...

375
00:23:04,508 --> 00:23:05,550
Oh, my.

376
00:23:05,551 --> 00:23:06,552
Sir!

377
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:16,061
I wasn't driving. That punk did it!

378
00:23:16,562 --> 00:23:18,355
Please calm down.

379
00:23:20,357 --> 00:23:22,067
You son of a gun!

380
00:23:24,737 --> 00:23:26,029
Min Seo.

381
00:23:26,030 --> 00:23:27,948
Kids, this...

382
00:23:28,741 --> 00:23:29,742
What's this?

383
00:23:30,534 --> 00:23:33,411
Ye Ji, go inside with Min Seo and lock the door.

384
00:23:33,412 --> 00:23:35,748
Run away from here, okay?

385
00:23:37,958 --> 00:23:40,001
- What are these for? - What do you think?

386
00:23:40,002 --> 00:23:41,461
Didn't you see the look in his eyes?

387
00:23:41,462 --> 00:23:43,213
He's going to kill us!

388
00:23:43,547 --> 00:23:45,256
We have to try something at least.

389
00:23:45,257 --> 00:23:46,884
There are four of us.

390
00:23:47,676 --> 00:23:49,719
Four? You mean, us?

391
00:23:49,720 --> 00:23:52,180
We've got two men with us now.

392
00:23:52,181 --> 00:23:54,141
Doesn't that give us a fighting chance?

393
00:24:00,272 --> 00:24:01,649
I'm sorry, sir.

394
00:24:02,608 --> 00:24:04,985
I'm sorry. I apologize.

395
00:24:07,446 --> 00:24:08,530
I'm sorry...

396
00:24:22,753 --> 00:24:25,880
Oh, my. We have to do something...

397
00:24:25,881 --> 00:24:28,968
Oh, boy. Goodness!

398
00:24:46,652 --> 00:24:49,070
Who are you people, really?

399
00:24:49,071 --> 00:24:50,238
- What... - Tell me.

400
00:24:50,239 --> 00:24:52,282
Us? We...

401
00:24:52,950 --> 00:24:54,750
We aren't anyone. We're just ordinary people.

402
00:24:54,910 --> 00:24:56,494
Let me guess. This was an accident too?

403
00:24:56,495 --> 00:24:57,578
- Yes, that too. - Yes.

404
00:24:57,579 --> 00:24:59,789
- That was also an accident. - It was.

405
00:24:59,790 --> 00:25:02,126
I know it's hard to believe, but it was.

406
00:25:08,841 --> 00:25:10,426
Let me ask you one thing.

407
00:25:11,844 --> 00:25:15,972
Why did you kill Sol and Choi Sang Cheol?

408
00:25:15,973 --> 00:25:16,974
Who sent you?

409
00:25:17,933 --> 00:25:19,475
- Kill them? - What...

410
00:25:19,476 --> 00:25:20,810
- Because of him... - Wait.

411
00:25:20,811 --> 00:25:22,645
- What do you mean, who sent us? - No.

412
00:25:22,646 --> 00:25:25,314
Listen, what happened to your brother was...

413
00:25:25,315 --> 00:25:27,191
truly an accident caused by Min Seo.

414
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:28,901
- No! - What do you mean, no?

415
00:25:28,902 --> 00:25:30,903
- These two buried Sol... - Excuse me?

416
00:25:30,904 --> 00:25:32,655
- in there. - Stop talking nonsense!

417
00:25:32,656 --> 00:25:33,740
- Horrible jerks. - She keeps...

418
00:25:33,741 --> 00:25:35,658
- making up ridiculous stories. - No.

419
00:25:35,659 --> 00:25:38,286
Fine, then.

420
00:25:38,287 --> 00:25:40,330
I'll just kill all of you darn people.

421
00:25:59,641 --> 00:26:01,310
- Dad! - Honey!

422
00:26:01,894 --> 00:26:02,894
- Min Seo. - Kids!

423
00:26:02,895 --> 00:26:03,896
- Ye Ji! - Jeez!

424
00:26:04,646 --> 00:26:05,898
Hey, you little punk!

425
00:26:39,389 --> 00:26:40,932
We're so sorry.

426
00:26:40,933 --> 00:26:43,185
But it's really all just a huge misunderstanding.

427
00:26:44,937 --> 00:26:46,438
- Honey! - Dad!

428
00:26:48,107 --> 00:26:49,233
Ye Ji!

429
00:27:12,214 --> 00:27:14,591
How dare you lay a finger on my kid?

430
00:28:24,494 --> 00:28:25,746
What...

431
00:28:50,229 --> 00:28:51,938
Do you think this is enough?

432
00:28:51,939 --> 00:28:53,023
Yes.

433
00:28:53,523 --> 00:28:55,901
I added one more bag this time.

434
00:29:13,752 --> 00:29:14,878
Are you okay?

435
00:29:51,581 --> 00:29:52,916
What do we do?

436
00:29:54,376 --> 00:29:56,669
If we take him to the hospital now...

437
00:29:56,670 --> 00:29:58,297
It'll complicate things...

438
00:30:02,509 --> 00:30:03,802
in many ways.

439
00:30:29,286 --> 00:30:33,122
Thank goodness, we stocked up on cement.

440
00:30:33,123 --> 00:30:34,499
Right, honey?

441
00:32:52,512 --> 00:32:54,763
(One month later)

442
00:32:54,764 --> 00:32:56,015
Yes.

443
00:32:56,016 --> 00:32:59,351
Look more into it and get back to me.

444
00:32:59,352 --> 00:33:00,353
Okay, bye.

445
00:33:01,521 --> 00:33:04,231
Sir, the registered owner of this car is Na Sol.

446
00:33:04,232 --> 00:33:05,524
Is it a woman?

447
00:33:05,525 --> 00:33:06,609
No, a man.

448
00:33:06,610 --> 00:33:09,111
But there's no report of the car being stolen,

449
00:33:09,112 --> 00:33:12,282
and his phone's been off since then, so we can't track his location.

450
00:33:14,034 --> 00:33:15,434
Smells like a homicide, doesn't it?

451
00:33:16,870 --> 00:33:20,207
Yes, but we won't know for sure until we pull the car up.

452
00:33:21,416 --> 00:33:22,917
What's taking them so long?

453
00:33:22,918 --> 00:33:25,504
Darn, when do I get to go home?

454
00:33:28,131 --> 00:33:31,176
They took the dashcam's memory card.

455
00:33:31,760 --> 00:33:33,303
They removed the aftermarket one,

456
00:33:33,762 --> 00:33:35,222
but the factory one is still there.

457
00:33:35,764 --> 00:33:37,307
- The factory one? - Here.

458
00:33:38,558 --> 00:33:40,684
It has a built-in one,

459
00:33:40,685 --> 00:33:42,646
but it's outdated, so he added a custom one.

460
00:33:44,439 --> 00:33:45,524
We won't know...

461
00:33:46,316 --> 00:33:49,193
if the built-in camera captured anything...

462
00:33:49,194 --> 00:33:50,570
until we extract the data.

463
00:33:50,987 --> 00:33:54,324
If we restore the data, can we get some footage?

464
00:33:54,950 --> 00:33:56,701
We'll have to give it a try.

465
00:33:57,661 --> 00:33:58,869
Sir.

466
00:33:58,870 --> 00:33:59,871
- Sir. - What?

467
00:34:01,456 --> 00:34:03,582
- About the car owner, Na Sol. - What about him?

468
00:34:03,583 --> 00:34:05,334
He has a twin brother...

469
00:34:05,335 --> 00:34:07,753
named Na Do.

470
00:34:07,754 --> 00:34:10,034
Apparently, they ran a private detective agency together.

471
00:34:10,590 --> 00:34:12,425
- A private detective agency? - Yes.

472
00:34:13,176 --> 00:34:15,094
The thing is, he is also missing.

473
00:34:15,095 --> 00:34:17,722
There's been zero activity on his phone and credit cards.

474
00:34:19,558 --> 00:34:21,142
Both of them?

475
00:34:23,603 --> 00:34:26,480
Track down their last known locations first.

476
00:34:26,481 --> 00:34:28,066
Last known locations, got it.

477
00:34:32,445 --> 00:34:33,696
Honey.

478
00:34:33,697 --> 00:34:35,865
Honey!

479
00:34:35,991 --> 00:34:38,576
Did you see this?

480
00:34:38,577 --> 00:34:40,203
You need to see this.

481
00:34:43,081 --> 00:34:47,126
A mid-sized sedan is being recovered from a reservoir.

482
00:34:47,127 --> 00:34:48,544
The vehicle's owner was identified...

483
00:34:48,545 --> 00:34:50,754
- as a private detective. - Isn't that him?

484
00:34:50,755 --> 00:34:53,842
He's been missing for 34 days.

485
00:34:54,342 --> 00:34:55,634
- Mr. Na was last seen... - Yes.

486
00:34:55,635 --> 00:34:58,075
- near an intersection convenience store. - The date matches.

487
00:34:58,555 --> 00:34:59,847
Police launched an investigation,

488
00:34:59,848 --> 00:35:01,641
- but he still... - A reservoir?

489
00:35:02,684 --> 00:35:04,185
What's that about?

490
00:35:04,644 --> 00:35:06,687
The police aren't...

491
00:35:06,688 --> 00:35:10,275
going to show up at our door, are they?

492
00:35:11,109 --> 00:35:14,737
Should we get our stories straight just in case?

493
00:35:14,738 --> 00:35:16,239
If the police ask questions...

494
00:35:17,949 --> 00:35:18,950
What?

495
00:35:20,035 --> 00:35:21,910
This is the Cheongnam Police.

496
00:35:21,911 --> 00:35:23,496
Could you open the door?

497
00:35:25,081 --> 00:35:26,207
Is anyone home?

498
00:35:45,977 --> 00:35:47,312
You don't remember?

499
00:35:49,939 --> 00:35:51,066
Still?

500
00:35:54,778 --> 00:35:57,697
You were the last people with Mr. Na Do.

501
00:35:59,032 --> 00:36:01,284
Around 5pm on April 8,

502
00:36:02,577 --> 00:36:04,412
you were at your vacation home, right?

503
00:36:05,121 --> 00:36:07,832
This footage is from right outside your vacation home.

504
00:36:15,006 --> 00:36:17,842
It's fine if you want to exercise your right to remain silent,

505
00:36:19,427 --> 00:36:22,471
but if you refuse to cooperate,

506
00:36:22,472 --> 00:36:25,058
I'll have to secure a warrant...

507
00:36:25,684 --> 00:36:28,978
and raid that property.

508
00:36:37,278 --> 00:36:38,988
I'll tell you everything.

509
00:36:41,282 --> 00:36:43,201
You should.

510
00:36:45,078 --> 00:36:46,287
Honey.

511
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:55,213
The truth is...

512
00:37:04,639 --> 00:37:05,890
To tell you the truth...

513
00:37:11,354 --> 00:37:12,605
I...

514
00:37:16,192 --> 00:37:17,777
Mr. Na Do...

515
00:37:34,294 --> 00:37:35,503
Jae Hong...

516
00:37:37,005 --> 00:37:38,757
That's Eun Bin's real name.

517
00:37:43,011 --> 00:37:45,491
Jae Hong was cheating on me with the neighbour across the road.

518
00:37:46,389 --> 00:37:47,599
What...

519
00:38:04,199 --> 00:38:06,743
What is this? They're...

520
00:38:13,541 --> 00:38:14,876
Mr. Na discovered...

521
00:38:15,877 --> 00:38:18,296
that the neighbour named Ahn Soo Jung...

522
00:38:18,838 --> 00:38:20,131
and Jae Hong...

523
00:38:20,715 --> 00:38:22,926
were going to the vacation home.

524
00:38:24,594 --> 00:38:28,139
He got there ahead of them.

525
00:38:52,288 --> 00:38:54,207
And I followed.

526
00:38:56,668 --> 00:38:58,920
(Ye Ji's House)

527
00:39:03,633 --> 00:39:05,176
Wow, you're so good.

528
00:39:05,426 --> 00:39:06,427
Really?

529
00:39:11,599 --> 00:39:12,683
Hong!

530
00:39:12,684 --> 00:39:14,686
Hey, Lim Jae Hong!

531
00:39:20,859 --> 00:39:22,110
But then,

532
00:39:23,653 --> 00:39:25,363
is Mr. Na...

533
00:39:26,781 --> 00:39:27,991
dead?

534
00:39:30,118 --> 00:39:32,203
What makes you think so?

535
00:39:32,996 --> 00:39:35,206
Well, you said...

536
00:39:35,874 --> 00:39:37,250
we were the last ones to see him.

537
00:39:40,670 --> 00:39:42,589
To be precise,

538
00:39:43,089 --> 00:39:44,757
his official status is missing.

539
00:39:48,344 --> 00:39:50,179
Have you perhaps...

540
00:39:51,556 --> 00:39:53,725
seen this man before,

541
00:39:54,851 --> 00:39:58,438
or did Mr. Na ever mention the name Ko Du Sik?

542
00:39:59,480 --> 00:40:01,482
I'm not so sure...

543
00:40:03,902 --> 00:40:05,236
Why do you ask?

544
00:40:09,324 --> 00:40:10,867
I said it wasn't me.

545
00:40:12,660 --> 00:40:15,163
Why the heck is everyone coming after me?

546
00:40:15,580 --> 00:40:17,748
- We have solid evidence... - You have no...

547
00:40:17,749 --> 00:40:19,042
that he planned to kill Mr. Na.

548
00:40:22,921 --> 00:40:25,714
- Evidence of murder? - What...

549
00:40:25,715 --> 00:40:27,425
Evidence of murder?

550
00:40:33,348 --> 00:40:34,640
Yes.

551
00:40:34,641 --> 00:40:37,434
Ko Du Sik tried to make contact with Mr. Na...

552
00:40:37,435 --> 00:40:39,979
on the day of the incident.

553
00:40:43,274 --> 00:40:46,319
It looks like he tailed Mr. Na's car.

554
00:40:48,071 --> 00:40:50,198
He caused a collision on purpose...

555
00:40:59,040 --> 00:41:02,377
likely with the intent to kill Mr. Na.

556
00:41:16,182 --> 00:41:17,684
Darn.

557
00:41:22,981 --> 00:41:25,984
You took good care of the car, right?

558
00:41:28,069 --> 00:41:29,153
Yes.

